From: NixOS Android devices contributors <nixos-android-devices@localhost>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 05:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: retain connector in debugfs private state

Local fix against Linux v7.3-rc4. Reading dp_test_active on Asphalt
triggered a NULL pointer dereference in msm_dp_test_active_show().
msm_dp_debug_init() receives the connector but never stores it, leaving
all three compliance-test readers and the writer with a NULL pointer.
Retain it alongside the link and panel before publishing the files.

Source: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v7.3-rc4/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_debug.c
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_debug.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_debug.c
index cf3838fcd..00fb1a7ba 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_debug.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_debug.c
@@ -216,6 +216,7 @@ int msm_dp_debug_init(struct device *dev, struct msm_dp_panel *panel,
 
 	debug->link = link;
 	debug->panel = panel;
+	debug->connector = connector;
 
 	debugfs_create_file("dp_debug", 0444, root,
 			debug, &msm_dp_debug_fops);
